Fleeing the swirling vortex, the ribbons embedded themselves into the polar skies. Nimbus searched the gales but found nothing. Yet, the next night, the heavens blazed with the first glowing auroras. The night sky's light was born, and to this day, the owl carries glowing silver speckles on her wings as a tribute to her daring theft.

