Myth: Long before the endless depths of the ocean knew the neon glow of bioluminescent life, the seafloor was trapped in a suffocating blanket of absolute pitch black. Deep within a petrified coral reef, a massive, greedy leviathan named Thalassa hoarded the ocean’s only pearl of deep-dawn, keeping the trenches locked in gloomy darkness.

A brave, translucent jellyfish named Pelagia wished to see the barren thermal vents flourish with light. Knowing the fearsome leviathan slumbered only when the surface was perfectly still, Pelagia drifted silently into the crushing shadows. She crept into the fortress and carefully wrapped her delicate tentacles around the radiant, sapphire pearl, illuminating her gossamer bell.

As Pelagia darted back toward the midnight zone, the furious leviathan awoke and unleashed a terrifying, swirling whirlpool. The chaotic currents battered Pelagia, sending her tumbling through the dense brine. The heavy pearl slipped from her grasp, shattering against a jagged obsidian vent into countless glowing droplets.

Where the sapphire droplets landed, the ocean depths erupted into vibrant, glowing colonies of luminescent creatures. Pelagia escaped, though her bell was forever marked with a glowing halo. Today, those scattered droplets are the deep sea’s radiant night-light, a tribute to a brave jellyfish's gift.
